a sequence of vertex deletions, edge deletions, and edge con tractions. The following alternative deﬁnition is
more relevant from the viewpoint of embeddings: a graph F is a minor of G if there is a mapping ψ that maps
each vertex of F to a connected subset of V (G) such that ψ (u)∩ ψ (v) = / 0 foru⁄= v, and if u,v∈ V (F) are
