there are two M-small sets S⊆ S′ violating consistency, i.e., sol (S)⁄⊆prS sol(S′). In this case, let s be a|S|-
tuple whose coordinates contain S in an arbitrary order and let us add the constraint ⟨s,prS sol(S′)⟩; it is clear
that sol(V ) does not change but|sol(S)| strictly decreases. We repeat this step until the instance b ecomes M-
consistent. Note that adding the new constraint can make a se t M-small that was not M-small before, thus we
need to rerun the algorithm of Lemma 4.3. To bound the number of iterations before M-consistency is reached,
