2 Preliminaries
Constraint satisfaction problems. We brieﬂy recall the most important notions related to CSP. F or more
background, see e.g., [26, 20].
Deﬁnition 2.1. An instance of a constraint satisfaction problem is a triple (V,D,C), where:
• V is a set of variables,
