codex
The compact route is now genuinely no-tool-accessible: it reads only the first two visible entries of each relation, and the final local run passes G1–G9(c), including five attacks at 0/8 and a verified 255-operation shortcut. The only incomplete evidence is the external four-vendor run; all three script-owned transcripts record quota errors and no model failures.
The generator, local gates, README, and all transcript files are complete. The required oracle and G9 model diagnostics were attempted repeatedly but OpenRouter rejected every draw with a quota-level HTTP 403, so no honest hardening verdict exists.
