codex
Implemented a native Track B CSP generator grounded in Definition 2.1 and the tractable-width results of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0911.0801).

Deliverables:

- [gen_0911_0801.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/gen_0911_0801.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0911.0801/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes every gate:

- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000
- Five attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, `O(nq)`
- Shipping reference cost: 81,920 operations
- Compact route: 255 operations
- Answer: 72 characters, 15 atoms
- Canonical-key tests: 40/40 invariant and 20/20 unrelated instances distinct

The only blocker is external: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo draw. The transcripts preserve those errors, but no oracle attempts occurred, so the result is not yet submission-complete and no hardness verdict is claimed. After restoring quota, rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_0911_0801.py
```

Then rerun the two G9 modes in separate scratch directories as documented in the README.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a0c45c8097188680f17885d43bc88e517a3808bb..37dedb8b195e287b368c474b2c42305aa3494f09
--- a/README.md
