notion of embedding where the images of distinct vertices ar e not necessarily disjoint, but can overlap in a
controlled way. We deﬁne such embeddings the following way. We say that two sets of vertices X ,Y⊆ V (H)
touch if either X∩Y⁄= / 0, or there is an edgee∈ E(H) intersecting both X and Y . An embedding of graph
G into hypergraph H is a mapping ψ that maps each vertex of H to a connected subset of V (G) such that if
u and v are adjacent in G, then ψ (u) and ψ (v) touch. The depth of a vertex v∈ V (H) in embedding ψ is
