@@ -1,20 +1,20 @@
-"""Parity-twisted functional-cycle CSPs from arXiv:0911.0801.
+"""Verified binary-CSP witnesses from cyclic XOR structure.
 
-Definition 2.1 of the paper represents a CSP by variables, a common finite
-domain, and extensionally listed relation tuples. This module uses exactly
-those native objects. Each component is a triangle of binary permutation
-relations. The relations are affine modulo a power of two in hidden
-coordinates, then transported through a fixed nonlinear domain relabelling.
+This module is grounded in Definition 2.1 and Section 7, Lemma 7.4 of
+arXiv:0911.0801.  It samples a Boolean witness first, constructs a full-rank
+cyclic system of ternary XOR equations around it, compiles every XOR equation
+to four 3-CNF clauses, and applies the paper's explicit reduction from 3-SAT
+to a domain-three binary CSP.  Extra compatible XOR equations enlarge the
+haystack without enlarging the returned witness.
 
-This is Track B. A standard algorithm scans every possible value around each
-functional cycle in O(n*q) table operations. Once the coordinate change is
-noticed, the three maps compose symbolically in constant work per component.
-Generation samples a fixed point first and never solves a generated instance.
+Generation is deterministic in ``(n, seed, params)``.  The module uses only
+the Python standard library, performs no file I/O, and prints nothing at
+import time.
 """
 
 from __future__ import annotations
 
